From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: give a FIQ on the T8132 way back
 its own window

The platform's catch vectors send all sixteen entries to one handler
that restarts WD2 by class: sync 145 s, SError 160 s, IRQ or FIQ
175 s. Timers and IPIs arrive as FIQs here, and ESR does not describe
an interrupt, so a FIQ read the same as an IRQ. Give FIQ 170 s.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 5825ddaa94..2ec411c6ef 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -2997,7 +2997,8 @@ static void apple_sleep_wait_still_on(struct apple_sleep *s)
  * vectors (before init_kernel_el) or the hyp stub's (after it), and both spin: the
  * reset then reads as the stub's 60 s. These vectors are in .text, used by PA while
  * the MMU is off and by kernel VA once _cpu_resume runs. Each restarts WD2 by class,
- * sync 145 s, SError 160 s, IRQ or FIQ 175 s, then leaves a record in PMU scratch
+ * sync 145 s, SError 160 s, IRQ 175 s, FIQ 170 s (timers and IPIs are FIQs here), then
+ * leaves a record in PMU scratch (ESR is stale for IRQ and FIQ: the window tells them)
  * 0xf804-0xf80e, which macsmc-reboot prints on the next boot: ISS[23:0], ELR[31:0],
  * FAR[23:0], then 0x80 | MMU on << 6 | EC in 0xf804 last. The SPMI writes come last:
  * WD2 resets the SoC either way.
@@ -3071,6 +3072,12 @@ asm(
 "\tcbz\tw13, 2f\n"
 "\tmovz\tw14, #0xea00\n"
 "\tmovk\tw14, #0xfa56, lsl #16\n"
+"\tcmp\tw13, #2\n"
+"\tb.ne\t5f\n"
+"\tmovz\tw14, #0xdc00\n"
+"\tmovk\tw14, #0xf32f, lsl #16\n"
+"\tb\t2f\n"
+"5:\n"
 "\tcmp\tw13, #3\n"
 "\tb.ne\t2f\n"
 "\tmovz\tw14, #0xc000\n"
-- 
